<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Afabet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1988</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-war-of-independence">Eritrean War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Afabet was fought in March 1988 around the town of Afabet in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-peoples-liberation-front">Eritrean People's Liberation Front</a> overran the headquarters of the Ethiopian army's Nadew Command. Several Ethiopian divisions were destroyed and large quantities of Soviet-supplied weapons captured. The victory shifted the balance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-war-of-independence">Eritrean War of Independence</a> decisively in the rebels' favour.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-afabet.jpg" alt="Battle of Afabet" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Destroyed_Ethiopian_tanks_after_battle_of_Afabet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
